#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike the Estimator primitive, the Sampler primitive does not have built-in support for error mitigation.\n"
"Several of the methods supported by the Estimator are specifically designed for expectation values, and hence are not applicable to the Sampler primitive. An exception is readout error mitigation, which is a highly effective method that is also applicable to the Sampler primitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi tulad ng Estimator primitive, ang Sampler primitive ay walang built-in na suporta para sa error mitigation.\n"
"Ilang mga pamamaraan na sinusuportahan ng Estimator ay partikular na dinisenyo para sa expectation values, at sa gayon ay hindi naaangkop sa Sampler primitive. Ang isang eksepsyon ay ang readout error mitigation, na isang lubhang epektibong pamamaraan na naaangkop din sa Sampler primitive.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [M3 Qiskit addon](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mthree/) "
"implements an efficient method for readout error mitigation. This tutorial "
"explains how to use the M3 Qiskit addon to mitigate readout error for the "
"Sampler primitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [M3 Qiskit addon](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mthree/) ay nag-"
"implement ng isang mahusay na pamamaraan para sa readout error mitigation. "
"Ang tutorial na ito ay nagpapaliwanag kung paano gamitin ang M3 Qiskit addon"
" upang mapawi ang readout error para sa Sampler primitive.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is readout error? {#what-is-readout-error}"
msgstr "Ano ang readout error? {#what-is-readout-error}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately before measurement, the state of a qubit register is\n"
"described by a superposition of computational basis states,\n"
"or by a density matrix.\n"
"Measurement of the qubit register into a classical bit register then proceeds in two steps.\n"
"First the quantum measurement proper is performed.\n"
"This means that the state of the qubit register\n"
"is projected onto a single basis state that is characterized\n"
"by a string of $1$s and $0$s.\n"
"The second step consists of reading the bitstring characterizing this basis state\n"
"and writing it into classical computer memory.\n"
"We call this step *readout*.\n"
"It turns out that the second step (readout) incurs more error than the first step (projection onto basis states).\n"
"This makes sense when you recall that readout requires detecting a microscopic\n"
"quantum state and amplifying it to the macroscopic realm. A readout resonator is coupled to\n"
"the (transmon) qubit, thereby experiencing a very small frequency shift. A microwave pulse\n"
"is then bounced off of the resonator, in turn experiencing small changes in its\n"
"characteristics.  The reflected pulse is then amplified and analyzed.  This is a delicate\n"
"process and is subject to a host of errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaagad bago ang pagsukat, ang estado ng isang qubit register ay\n"
"inilarawan ng isang superposition ng computational basis states,\n"
"o ng isang density matrix.\n"
"Ang pagsukat ng qubit register tungo sa isang classical bit register ay umuusad sa dalawang hakbang.\n"
"Una, ang tunay na quantum measurement ay isinasagawa.\n"
"Nangangahulugan ito na ang estado ng qubit register\n"
"ay naipro-project sa isang solong basis state na nailalarawan\n"
"ng isang string ng $1$s at $0$s.\n"
"Ang ikalawang hakbang ay binubuo ng pagbasa sa bitstring na naglalarawan ng basis state na ito\n"
"at pagsusulat nito sa classical computer memory.\n"
"Tinatawag natin ang hakbang na ito na *readout*.\n"
"Lumalabas na ang ikalawang hakbang (readout) ay may mas maraming error kaysa sa unang hakbang (projection sa basis states).\n"
"Makatuwirang isipin ito kung aalalahanin ninyo na ang readout ay nangangailangan ng pagtuklas sa isang microscopic\n"
"quantum state at pagpapalakas nito tungo sa macroscopic realm. Ang readout resonator ay nakakonekta sa\n"
"(transmon) qubit, at dahil dito ay nakakaranas ng napakaliit na frequency shift. Ang isang microwave pulse\n"
"ay ibinabato pabalik mula sa resonator, na naman ay nakakaranas ng maliliit na pagbabago sa\n"
"katangian nito. Ang na-reflect na pulse ay pinapalakas at sinusuri. Ito ay isang delikadong\n"
"proseso at napapailalim sa maraming uri ng errors.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The important point is that, while both quantum measurement and readout are subject to error, the\n"
"latter incurs the dominant error, called readout error, which is the focus in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mahalagang punto ay na, habang parehong quantum measurement at readout ay napapailalim sa error, ang\n"
"huli ay may mas nangingibabaw na error, na tinatawag na readout error, na siyang pokus sa tutorial na ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical background {#theoretical-background}"
msgstr "Teoretikal na kaligiran {#theoretical-background}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the sampled bitstring (stored in classical memory) differs from the bitstring characterizing\n"
"the projected quantum state, we say that a readout error has occurred.\n"
"These errors are observed to be random and uncorrelated from sample to sample.\n"
"It has proven useful to model readout error as a _noisy classical channel_.\n"
"That is, for every pair of\n"
"bitstrings $i$ and $j$, there is a fixed probability that a true value of $j$ will\n"
"be incorrectly read as $i$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang sampled bitstring (na naka-imbak sa classical memory) ay naiiba mula sa bitstring na naglalarawan sa\n"
"projected quantum state, sinasabi natin na naganap ang isang readout error.\n"
"Ang mga error na ito ay napapansin na random at walang korelasyon mula sa sample hanggang sample.\n"
"Napatunayang kapaki-pakinabang na i-modelo ang readout error bilang isang _noisy classical channel_.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, para sa bawat pares ng\n"
"bitstrings $i$ at $j$, may nakapirming probabilidad na ang tunay na halaga ng $j$ ay\n"
"mali ang pagbasa bilang $i$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More precisely, for every pair of bitstrings $(i, j)$, there is a (conditional) probability ${M}_{i,j}$\n"
"that $i$ is read, given that the true value is $j.$\n"
"That is,\n"
"$$\n"
"    {M}_{i,j} =  \\Pr(\\text{readout value is } i | \\text{true value is } j)\n"
"    \\text{ for } i,j \\in (0,...,2^n - 1), \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $n$ is the number of bits in the readout register.\n"
"For concreteness, we assume that $i$ is a decimal integer whose binary representation is\n"
"the bitstring that labels the computational basis states.\n"
"We call the $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrix ${M}$ the _assignment matrix_.\n"
"For fixed true value $j$, summing the probability over all noisy outcomes $i$ must give $1$. That is\n"
"$$\n"
"    \\sum_{i=0}^{2^n - 1} {M}_{i,j} = 1 \\text{ for all } j\n"
"$$\n"
"A matrix with no negative entries that satisfies (1) is called\n"
"_left-stochastic_.\n"
"A left-stochastic matrix is also called _column-stochastic_ because each of its columns sums to $1$.\n"
"We experimentally determine approximate values for each element ${M}_{i,j}$ by\n"
"repeatedly preparing each basis state $|j \\rangle$ and then computing the frequencies\n"
"of the occurrence of sampled bitstrings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas tiyak na paraan, para sa bawat pares ng bitstrings $(i, j)$, may isang (conditional) probability ${M}_{i,j}$\n"
"na ang $i$ ay mabasa, kung ibinigay na ang tunay na halaga ay $j.$\n"
"Iyon ay,\n"
"$$\n"
"    {M}_{i,j} =  \\Pr(\\text{readout value is } i | \\text{true value is } j)\n"
"    \\text{ for } i,j \\in (0,...,2^n - 1), \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan $n$ ay ang bilang ng bits sa readout register.\n"
"Para sa concreteness, ipinagpapalagay natin na ang $i$ ay isang decimal integer na ang binary representation ay\n"
"ang bitstring na naglalabel sa computational basis states.\n"
"Tinatawag natin ang $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrix ${M}$ na _assignment matrix_.\n"
"Para sa nakapirming tunay na halaga $j$, ang pagbubuod ng probabilidad sa lahat ng maingay na kinalabasan $i$ ay dapat magbigay ng $1$. Iyon ay\n"
"$$\n"
"    \\sum_{i=0}^{2^n - 1} {M}_{i,j} = 1 \\text{ for all } j\n"
"$$\n"
"Ang isang matrix na walang negatibong entries na nakakatugon sa (1) ay tinatawag na\n"
"_left-stochastic_.\n"
"Ang left-stochastic matrix ay tinatawag ding _column-stochastic_ dahil ang bawat column nito ay may kabuuan na $1$.\n"
"Eksperimental na tinutukoy natin ang approximate values para sa bawat element ${M}_{i,j}$ sa pamamagitan ng\n"
"paulit-ulit na paghahanda sa bawat basis state $|j \\rangle$ at pagkatapos ay pagkompyut ng frequencies\n"
"ng pagkakaroon ng sampled bitstrings.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If an experiment involves estimating a probability distribution over output bitstrings by repeated sampling,\n"
"then we can use ${M}$ to mitigate readout error at the level of the distribution.\n"
"The first step is to repeat a fixed circuit of interest many times,\n"
"creating a histogram of sampled bitstrings.\n"
"The normalized histogram is the measured probability distribution over\n"
"the $2^n$ possible bitstrings, which we denote by ${\\tilde{p}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{2^n}$.\n"
"The (estimated) probability ${{\\tilde{p}}}_i$ of sampling bitstring $i$\n"
"is equal to the sum over all true bitstrings $j$, each weighted by\n"
"the probability that it is mistaken for $i$.\n"
"This statement in matrix form is\n"
"$$\n"
"    {\\tilde{p}} = {M} {\\vec{p}}, \\tag{2},\n"
"$$\n"
"where ${\\vec{p}}$ is the true distribution. In words, the readout error has the effect of multiplying\n"
"the ideal distribution over bitstrings ${\\vec{p}}$ by the assignment matrix ${M}$ to\n"
"produce the observed distribution ${\\tilde{p}}$.\n"
"We have measured ${\\tilde{p}}$ and ${M}$, but have no direct access to ${\\vec{p}}$. In principle, we will\n"
"obtain the true distribution of bitstrings for our circuit\n"
"by solving equation (2) for ${\\vec{p}}$ numerically.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang isang eksperimento ay nagsasangkot ng pagtatantya sa isang probability distribution sa output bitstrings sa pamamagitan ng paulit-ulit na pag-sample,\n"
"kung gayon ay maaari nating gamitin ang ${M}$ upang mapawi ang readout error sa antas ng distribution.\n"
"Ang unang hakbang ay ulitin ang isang nakapirming circuit ng interes nang maraming beses,\n"
"lumilikha ng histogram ng sampled bitstrings.\n"
"Ang normalized histogram ay ang sinukat na probability distribution sa\n"
"$2^n$ posibleng bitstrings, na tinutukoy natin bilang ${\\tilde{p}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{2^n}$.\n"
"Ang (tinantyang) probability ${{\\tilde{p}}}_i$ ng pag-sample ng bitstring $i$\n"
"ay katumbas ng kabuuan sa lahat ng tunay na bitstrings $j$, bawat isa ay may timbang ng\n"
"probabilidad na ito ay pagkakamali para sa $i$.\n"
"Ang pahayag na ito sa matrix form ay\n"
"$$\n"
"    {\\tilde{p}} = {M} {\\vec{p}}, \\tag{2},\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang ${\\vec{p}}$ ay ang tunay na distribution. Sa mga salita, ang readout error ay may epekto ng pagpaparami\n"
"ng ideal distribution sa bitstrings ${\\vec{p}}$ gamit ang assignment matrix ${M}$ upang\n"
"makagawa ng nakitang distribution ${\\tilde{p}}$.\n"
"Nasukat natin ang ${\\tilde{p}}$ at ${M}$, ngunit walang direktang access sa ${\\vec{p}}$. Sa prinsipyo, makukuha natin\n"
"ang tunay na distribution ng bitstrings para sa ating circuit\n"
"sa pamamagitan ng paglutas ng equation (2) para sa ${\\vec{p}}$ nang numerical.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we move on, it's worth noting some important features of this naive "
"approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago tayo magpatuloy, sulit na pansinin ang ilang mahalagang katangian ng "
"naive approach na ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In practice, equation (2) is not solved by inverting ${M}$. Linear algebra\n"
"routines in software libraries employ methods that are more stable, accurate, and efficient.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa praktika, ang equation (2) ay hindi nilulutas sa pamamagitan ng pag-invert sa ${M}$. Ang linear algebra\n"
"routines sa software libraries ay gumagamit ng mga pamamaraang mas stable, tumpak, at mahusay.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When estimating ${M}$, we assumed that only readout errors occurred. In particular,\n"
"we assume there were no state preparation and quantum measurement errors —\n"
"or at least that they were otherwise mitigated.\n"
"To the extent that this is a good assumption, ${M}$ really represents\n"
"only readout error. But when we _use_ ${M}$ to correct a measured distribution\n"
"over bitstrings, we make no such assumption. In fact, we expect an interesting\n"
"circuit to introduce noise, for instance, gate errors. The \"true\" distribution\n"
"still includes effects from any errors that are not otherwise mitigated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag tinatantya ang ${M}$, ipinagpalagay natin na readout errors lamang ang naganap. Sa partikular,\n"
"ipinagpapalagay natin na walang state preparation at quantum measurement errors —\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This method, while useful in some circumstances, suffers from a few "
"limitations.\n"
msgstr ""
"  o hindi bababa sa ito ay napawi sa ibang paraan.\n"
"  Hanggang sa ito ay isang mabuting pagpapalagay, ang ${M}$ ay tunay na kumakatawan lamang\n"
"  sa readout error. Ngunit kapag _ginagamit_ natin ang ${M}$ upang itama ang isang sinukat na distribution\n"
"  sa bitstrings, hindi natin ginagawa ang gayong pagpapalagay. Sa katunayan, inaasahan natin ang isang kawili-wiling\n"
"  circuit na magpakilala ng ingay, halimbawa, gate errors. Ang \"tunay\" na distribution\n"
"  ay kasama pa rin ang mga epekto mula sa anumang errors na hindi napawi sa ibang paraan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The space and time resources needed to estimate ${M}$ grow exponentially in $n$:\n"
"- The estimation of ${M}$ and ${\\tilde{p}}$ is subject to statistical error due to finite sampling.\n"
"  This noise can be made as small as desired\n"
"  at the cost of more shots (up to the timescale of drifting hardware parameters\n"
"  that result in systematic errors in ${M}$).\n"
"  However, if no assumptions are made on the bitstrings observed\n"
"  when performing mitigation, the number of shots required to estimate ${M}$ grows\n"
"  at least exponentially in $n$.\n"
"- ${M}$ is a $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrix.\n"
"  When $n>10$, the amount of memory required to store ${M}$ is\n"
"  greater than the memory available in a powerful laptop.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pamamaraang ito, bagaman kapaki-pakinabang sa ilang pangyayari, ay "
"nakakaranas ng ilang limitasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Further limitations are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang space at time resources na kailangan upang tantiyahin ang ${M}$ ay lumalaki nang exponential sa $n$:\n"
"- Ang pagtatantya ng ${M}$ at ${\\tilde{p}}$ ay napapailalim sa statistical error dahil sa finite sampling.\n"
"  Ang ingay na ito ay maaaring gawing kasing liit ng nais\n"
"  sa gastos ng mas maraming shots (hanggang sa timescale ng drifting hardware parameters\n"
"  na nagreresulta sa systematic errors sa ${M}$).\n"
"  Gayunpaman, kung walang mga pagpapalagay na ginawa sa bitstrings na nakikita\n"
"  kapag nagsasagawa ng mitigation, ang bilang ng shots na kinakailangan upang tantiyahin ang ${M}$ ay lumalaki\n"
"  hindi bababa sa exponential sa $n$.\n"
"- Ang ${M}$ ay isang $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrix.\n"
"  Kapag $n>10$, ang dami ng memory na kinakailangan upang mag-imbak ng ${M}$ ay\n"
"  mas malaki kaysa sa memory na available sa isang makapangyarihang laptop.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recovered distribution ${\\vec{p}}$ may have one\n"
"or more negative probabilities (while still summing to one). One solution\n"
"is to minimize $||{M} {\\vec{p}} - {\\tilde{p}}||^2$ subject to the constraint that\n"
"each entry in ${\\vec{p}}$ be non-negative. However, the runtime of such a\n"
"method is orders of magnitude longer than directly solving equation (2).\n"
msgstr "Ang nabalik na distribution ${\\vec{p}}$ ay maaaring may isa\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This mitigation procedure works on the level of a probability distribution\n"
"over bitstrings. In particular, it cannot correct an error in an individual\n"
"observed bitstring.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit M3 addon: Scaling to longer bitstrings {#qiskit-m3-addon-scaling-to-"
"longer-bitstrings}"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit M3 addon: Scaling sa mas mahabang bitstrings {#qiskit-m3-addon-"
"scaling-to-longer-bitstrings}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Solving equation (2) using standard numeric linear algebra routines is limited to bitstrings no longer than about 10 bits. M3, however, can handle much longer bitstrings. Two key properties of M3 that make this possible are:\n"
"- Correlations in readout error of order three and higher among collections of bits\n"
"  are assumed to be negligible and are ignored. In principle, at the cost of more shots,\n"
"  one could estimate higher correlations as well.\n"
"- Rather than constructing ${M}$ explicitly, we use a much smaller effective matrix that records\n"
"  probabilities only for bitstrings collected when constructing ${\\tilde{p}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paglutas ng equation (2) gamit ang standard numeric linear algebra routines ay limitado sa bitstrings na hindi hihigit sa mga 10 bits. Ang M3, gayunpaman, ay kayang hawakan ang mas mahabang bitstrings. Ang dalawang pangunahing katangian ng M3 na ginagawang posible ito ay:\n"
"- Ang mga korelasyon sa readout error ng order three at mas mataas sa mga koleksyon ng bits\n"
"  ay ipinagpapalagay na negligible at binabalewala. Sa prinsipyo, sa gastos ng mas maraming shots,\n"
"  maaari ding tantiyahin ang mas mataas na korelasyon.\n"
"- Sa halip na tuwiran na bumuo ng ${M}$, ginagamit natin ang mas maliit na effective matrix na nagrerekord\n"
"  ng mga probabilidad lamang para sa bitstrings na nakolekta kapag bumubuo ng ${\\tilde{p}}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "At a high level, the procedure works as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mataas na antas, ang pamamaraan ay gumagana sa sumusunod na paraan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we construct building blocks from which we can construct a simplified, effective, description of ${M}$.\n"
"Then, we repeatedly run the circuit of interest and collect bitstrings which we use to construct\n"
"both ${\\tilde{p}}$ and, with the help of the building blocks, an effective ${M}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, bumubuo tayo ng mga building blocks kung saan tayo maaaring bumuo ng isang pinasimpleng, effective, na paglalarawan ng ${M}$.\n"
"Pagkatapos, paulit-ulit nating pinapatakbo ang circuit ng interes at nakolekta ang bitstrings na ginagamit natin upang bumuo\n"
"ng parehong ${\\tilde{p}}$ at, sa tulong ng mga building blocks, isang effective ${M}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More precisely,\n"
"- Single-qubit assignment matrices are estimated for each qubit. To do this, we repeatedly\n"
"  prepare the qubit register in the all-zero state $|0 ... 0 \\rangle$ and then in the all-one\n"
"  state $|1 ... 1 \\rangle$, and record the probability for each qubit that it is read\n"
"  incorrectly.\n"
"- Correlations of order three and higher are assumed to be negligible and are ignored.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas tiyak na paraan,\n"
"- Ang mga single-qubit assignment matrices ay tinatantya para sa bawat qubit. Upang gawin ito, paulit-ulit tayong\n"
"  naghahanda ng qubit register sa all-zero state $|0 ... 0 \\rangle$ at pagkatapos ay sa all-one\n"
"  state $|1 ... 1 \\rangle$, at nagrerekord ng probabilidad para sa bawat qubit na ito ay maling\n"
"  nabasa.\n"
"- Ang mga korelasyon ng order three at mas mataas ay ipinagpapalagay na negligible at binabalewala.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Instead we construct a number $n$ of $2 \\times 2$ single-qubit\n"
"  assignment matrices, and a number $n(n-1)/2$ of $4 \\times 4$ two-qubit assignment\n"
"  matrices. These one- and two-qubit assignment matrices are stored for later\n"
"  use.\n"
"- After repeatedly sampling a circuit to construct ${\\tilde{p}}$,\n"
"  we construct an effective approximation to ${M}$ using only\n"
"  bitstrings that are sampled when constructing ${\\tilde{p}}$. This effective matrix\n"
"  is built using the single- and two-qubit matrices described in the previous item.\n"
"  The linear dimension of this matrix is at most of the order of the number\n"
"  of shots used in constructing ${\\tilde{p}}$, which is much smaller than\n"
"  the dimension $2^n$ of the full assignment matrix ${M}$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa halip, bumubuo tayo ng bilang $n$ ng $2 \\times 2$ single-qubit\n"
"  assignment matrices, at bilang $n(n-1)/2$ ng $4 \\times 4$ two-qubit assignment\n"
"  matrices. Ang mga one- at two-qubit assignment matrices na ito ay naka-imbak para sa susunod na\n"
"  paggamit.\n"
"- Matapos paulit-ulit na mag-sample ng isang circuit upang bumuo ng ${\\tilde{p}}$,\n"
"  bumubuo tayo ng isang effective approximation sa ${M}$ gamit lamang\n"
"  ang bitstrings na na-sample kapag bumubuo ng ${\\tilde{p}}$. Ang effective matrix na ito\n"
"  ay binuo gamit ang mga single- at two-qubit matrices na inilarawan sa nakaraang item.\n"
"  Ang linear dimension ng matrix na ito ay hindi hihigit sa order ng bilang\n"
"  ng shots na ginamit sa pagbuo ng ${\\tilde{p}}$, na mas maliit pa kaysa\n"
"  dimension $2^n$ ng buong assignment matrix ${M}$ .\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For technical details on M3, you can refer to [*Scalable Mitigation of "
"Measurement Errors on Quantum "
"Computers*](https://journals.aps.org/prxquantum/abstract/10.1103/PRXQuantum.2.040326).\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mga teknikal na detalye tungkol sa M3, maaari ninyong tingnan ang "
"[*Scalable Mitigation of Measurement Errors on Quantum "
"Computers*](https://journals.aps.org/prxquantum/abstract/10.1103/PRXQuantum.2.040326).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Application of M3 to a quantum algorithm {#application-of-m3-to-a-quantum-"
"algorithm}"
msgstr ""
"Aplikasyon ng M3 sa isang quantum algorithm {#application-of-m3-to-a-"
"quantum-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll apply M3's readout mitigation to the hidden shift problem. The hidden "
"shift problem, and closely related problems such as the [hidden subgroup "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_subgroup_problem), were "
"originally conceived in a fault-tolerant setting (more precisely, before "
"fault-tolerant QPUs were proved to be possible!). But they are studied with "
"available processors as well. An example of algorithmic exponential speedup "
"obtained for a variant of the hidden shift problem obtained on 127-qubit "
"IBM&reg; QPUs can be found in [this "
"paper](https://journals.aps.org/prx/accepted/a9074K06A8e1590147da9c69f8c4b64c28247be5a)"
" ([arXiv version](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.07934)).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ilalapat natin ang readout mitigation ng M3 sa hidden shift problem. Ang "
"hidden shift problem, at mga malapit na nauugnay na problema tulad ng "
"[hidden subgroup "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_subgroup_problem), ay orihinal"
" na nabuo sa fault-tolerant setting (sa mas tiyak na paraan, bago pa "
"napatunayan na posible ang fault-tolerant QPUs!). Ngunit pinag-aaralan din "
"ang mga ito gamit ang mga available processors. Ang isang halimbawa ng "
"algorithmic exponential speedup na nakuha para sa isang variant ng hidden "
"shift problem na nakuha sa 127-qubit IBM&reg; QPUs ay matatagpuan sa [paper "
"na "
"ito](https://journals.aps.org/prx/accepted/a9074K06A8e1590147da9c69f8c4b64c28247be5a)"
" ([arXiv version](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.07934)).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following, all arithmetic is Boolean.\n"
"That is, for $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2 = \\{0, 1\\}$, addition, $a + b$ is the logical XOR function.\n"
"Furthermore, multiplication $a \\times b$ (or $a b$) is the logical AND function. For $x, y \\in \\{0, 1\\}^n$,\n"
"$x + y$ is defined by bitwise application of XOR.\n"
"The dot product $\\cdot: {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_2$ is defined\n"
"by $x \\cdot y = \\sum_i x_i y_i$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa sumusunod, lahat ng arithmetic ay Boolean.\n"
"Iyon ay, para sa $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2 = \\{0, 1\\}$, addition, $a + b$ ay ang logical XOR function.\n"
"Bukod pa rito, multiplication $a \\times b$ (o $a b$) ay ang logical AND function. Para sa $x, y \\in \\{0, 1\\}^n$,\n"
"$x + y$ ay tinukoy sa pamamagitan ng bitwise application ng XOR.\n"
"Ang dot product $\\cdot: {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_2$ ay tinukoy\n"
"sa pamamagitan ng $x \\cdot y = \\sum_i x_i y_i$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hadamard operator and Fourier transform {#hadamard-operator-and-fourier-"
"transform}"
msgstr ""
"Hadamard operator at Fourier transform {#hadamard-operator-and-fourier-"
"transform}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In implementing quantum algorithms, it is very common to use the Hadamard operator as a Fourier transform.\n"
"The computational basis states are sometimes called _classical states_. They stand in\n"
"a one-to-one relation to the classical bitstrings.\n"
"The $n$-qubit Hadamard operator on classical states can be viewed as a Fourier transform on the Boolean hypercube:\n"
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x,y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n}} (-1)^{x \\cdot y} {|{y}\\rangle}{\\langle{x}|}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Consider a state ${|{s}\\rangle}$ corresponding to fixed bitstring $s$.\n"
"Applying $H^{\\otimes n}$, and using ${\\langle {x}|{s}\\rangle} = \\delta_{x,s}$,\n"
"we see that the Fourier transform of ${|{s}\\rangle}$ can be written as\n"
"$$\n"
"   H^{\\otimes n} {|{s}\\rangle} =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n}} (-1)^{s \\cdot y} {|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pag-implement ng mga quantum algorithms, napaka-karaniwan na gamitin ang Hadamard operator bilang isang Fourier transform.\n"
"Ang computational basis states ay kung minsan ay tinatawag na _classical states_. Sila ay nasa\n"
"one-to-one relation sa classical bitstrings.\n"
"Ang $n$-qubit Hadamard operator sa classical states ay maaaring tingnan bilang isang Fourier transform sa Boolean hypercube:\n"
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x,y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n}} (-1)^{x \\cdot y} {|{y}\\rangle}{\\langle{x}|}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Isaalang-alang ang isang state ${|{s}\\rangle}$ na tumutugma sa nakapirming bitstring $s$.\n"
"Sa paglalapat ng $H^{\\otimes n}$, at paggamit ng ${\\langle {x}|{s}\\rangle} = \\delta_{x,s}$,\n"
"nakikita natin na ang Fourier transform ng ${|{s}\\rangle}$ ay maaaring isulat bilang\n"
"$$\n"
"   H^{\\otimes n} {|{s}\\rangle} =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n}} (-1)^{s \\cdot y} {|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hadamard is its own inverse, that is,\n"
" $H^{\\otimes n} H^{\\otimes n} = (H H)^{\\otimes n} = I^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"Thus, the inverse Fourier transform is the same operator, $H^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"Explicitly, we have,\n"
"$$\n"
"  {|{s}\\rangle} =  H^{\\otimes n} H^{\\otimes n} {|{s}\\rangle}  =  H^{\\otimes n} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n}} (-1)^{s \\cdot y} {|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Hadamard ay sariling inverse, iyon ay,\n"
" $H^{\\otimes n} H^{\\otimes n} = (H H)^{\\otimes n} = I^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"Kaya, ang inverse Fourier transform ay ang parehong operator, $H^{\\otimes n}$.\n"
"Sa malinaw na paraan, mayroon tayo,\n"
"$$\n"
"  {|{s}\\rangle} =  H^{\\otimes n} H^{\\otimes n} {|{s}\\rangle}  =  H^{\\otimes n} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^n}} (-1)^{s \\cdot y} {|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The hidden shift problem {#the-hidden-shift-problem}"
msgstr "Ang hidden shift problem {#the-hidden-shift-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We consider a simple example of a _hidden shift problem_.\n"
"The problem is to identify a constant shift in the input to a function.\n"
"The function we consider is the dot product. It is the simplest member\n"
"of a large class of functions that admit a quantum speedup for the hidden shift\n"
"problem via techniques similar to those presented below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang natin ang isang simpleng halimbawa ng isang _hidden shift problem_.\n"
"Ang problema ay kilalanin ang isang constant shift sa input sa isang function.\n"
"Ang function na ating isaalang-alang ay ang dot product. Ito ay ang pinakasimpleng miyembro\n"
"ng isang malaking klase ng functions na tumatanggap ng quantum speedup para sa hidden shift\n"
"problem sa pamamagitan ng mga teknikang katulad ng mga ipinakita sa ibaba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $x,y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}$ be bitstrings of length $m$.\n"
"We define ${f}: {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\times {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\rightarrow \\{-1,1\\}$ by\n"
"$$\n"
"  {f}(x, y) = (-1)^{x \\cdot y}.\n"
"$$\n"
"  Let $a,b \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}$ be fixed bitstrings of length $m$.\n"
"  We furthermore define $g: {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\times {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\rightarrow \\{-1,1\\}$ by\n"
"$$\n"
"  g(x, y) = {f}(x+a, y+b) = (-1)^{(x+a) \\cdot (y+b)},\n"
"  $$\n"
"  where $a$ and $b$ are (hidden) parameters.\n"
"  We are given two black boxes, one implementing $f$, and the other $g$.\n"
"  We suppose that we know that they compute the functions defined above, except that we know\n"
"  neither $a$ nor $b$. The game is to determine the hidden bitstrings (shifts)\n"
"  $a$ and $b$ by making queries to $f$ and $g$. It's clear that if we play the game classically,\n"
"  we need $O(2m)$ queries to determine $a$ and $b$. For example, we can query $g$ with all pairs of strings such that one element of the pair is all zeros, and the other element has exactly one element set to $1$.\n"
"  On each query, we learn one element of either $a$ or $b$.\n"
"  However, we will see that, if the black boxes are implemented as quantum circuits, we can\n"
"  determine $a$ and $b$ with a single query to each of $f$ and $g$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hayaan ang $x,y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}$ na mga bitstrings ng haba $m$.\n"
"Tinukoy natin ang ${f}: {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\times {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\rightarrow \\{-1,1\\}$ bilang\n"
"$$\n"
"  {f}(x, y) = (-1)^{x \\cdot y}.\n"
"$$\n"
"  Hayaan ang $a,b \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}$ na nakapirming bitstrings ng haba $m$.\n"
"  Bukod pa rito, tinukoy natin ang $g: {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\times {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m} \\rightarrow \\{-1,1\\}$ bilang\n"
"$$\n"
"  g(x, y) = {f}(x+a, y+b) = (-1)^{(x+a) \\cdot (y+b)},\n"
"  $$\n"
"  kung saan ang $a$ at $b$ ay (nakatagong) parameters.\n"
"  Binigyan tayo ng dalawang black boxes, isa ay nag-implement ng $f$, at ang isa pa ay $g$.\n"
"  Ipinagpapalagay natin na alam natin na kinocompute nila ang mga function na tinukoy sa itaas, maliban sa hindi natin alam\n"
"  ang $a$ ni $b$. Ang laro ay upang matukoy ang mga nakatagong bitstrings (shifts)\n"
"  $a$ at $b$ sa pamamagitan ng paggawa ng mga query sa $f$ at $g$. Malinaw na kung nilalaro natin ang laro nang classical,\n"
"  kailangan natin ng $O(2m)$ queries upang matukoy ang $a$ at $b$. Halimbawa, maaari nating i-query ang $g$ sa lahat ng pares ng strings na ang isang elemento ng pares ay lahat ay zero, at ang iba pang elemento ay may eksaktong isang elemento na naka-set sa $1$.\n"
"  Sa bawat query, matututuhan natin ang isang elemento ng alinman sa $a$ o $b$.\n"
"  Gayunpaman, makikita natin na, kung ang mga black boxes ay ipinatupad bilang quantum circuits, maaari nating\n"
"  matukoy ang $a$ at $b$ sa isang solong query sa bawat isa sa $f$ at $g$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In the context of algorithmic complexity, a black box is called an _oracle_.\n"
"  In addition to being opaque, an oracle has the property that it consumes the input and\n"
"  produces the output instantly, adding nothing to the complexity budget of the algorithm\n"
"  in which it is embedded. In fact, in the case at hand, the oracles implementing $f$ and\n"
"  $g$ will be seen to be efficient.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa konteksto ng algorithmic complexity, ang isang black box ay tinatawag na _oracle_.\n"
"  Bilang karagdagan sa pagiging opaque, ang isang oracle ay may katangiang kinokonsumo nito ang input at\n"
"  gumagawa ng output kaagad, hindi nagdadagdag ng anuman sa complexity budget ng algorithm\n"
"  kung saan ito ay nakabaon. Sa katunayan, sa kasong ito, ang mga oracles na nag-implement ng $f$ at\n"
"  $g$ ay makikitang mahusay.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuits for $f$ and $g$ {#quantum-circuits-for-f-and-g}"
msgstr "Quantum circuits para sa $f$ at $g$ {#quantum-circuits-for-f-and-g}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We need the following ingredients in order to implement $f$ and $g$ as "
"quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kailangan natin ng mga sumusunod na sangkap upang i-implement ang $f$ at $g$"
" bilang quantum circuits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For single-qubit classical states ${|{x_1}\\rangle}, {|{y_1}\\rangle}$, with $x_1,y_1 \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2$,\n"
"the controlled-$Z$ gate ${CZ}$ may be written as\n"
"$$\n"
"{CZ} {|{x_1}\\rangle}{|{y_1}\\rangle}{x_1} = (-1)^{x_1 y_1} {|{x_1}\\rangle}{x_1}{|{y_1}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"We will operate with $m$ CZ gates, one on $(x_1, y_1)$, and one on $(x_2, y_2)$, and so on, through $(x_m, y_m)$.\n"
"We call this operator ${CZ}_{x,y}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa single-qubit classical states ${|{x_1}\\rangle}, {|{y_1}\\rangle}$, na may $x_1,y_1 \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2$,\n"
"ang controlled-$Z$ gate ${CZ}$ ay maaaring isulat bilang\n"
"$$\n"
"{CZ} {|{x_1}\\rangle}{|{y_1}\\rangle}{x_1} = (-1)^{x_1 y_1} {|{x_1}\\rangle}{x_1}{|{y_1}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Gagana tayo gamit ang $m$ CZ gates, isa sa $(x_1, y_1)$, at isa sa $(x_2, y_2)$, at iba pa, hanggang $(x_m, y_m)$.\n"
"Tinatawag natin ang operator na ito na ${CZ}_{x,y}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$U_f = {CZ}_{x,y}$ is a quantum version of ${f} = {f}(x,y)$:\n"
"$$\n"
"%\\CZ_{x,y} {|#1\\rangle}{z} =\n"
"U_f {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = {CZ}_{x,y} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = (-1)^{x \\cdot y}  {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $U_f = {CZ}_{x,y}$ ay isang quantum version ng ${f} = {f}(x,y)$:\n"
"$$\n"
"%\\CZ_{x,y} {|#1\\rangle}{z} =\n"
"U_f {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = {CZ}_{x,y} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = (-1)^{x \\cdot y}  {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also need to implement a bitstring shift.\n"
"We denote the operator on the $x$ register $X^{a_1}\\cdots X^{a_m}$ by $X_a$\n"
"and likewise on the $y$ register $X_b =  X^{b_1}\\cdots X^{b_m}$.\n"
"These operators apply $X$ wherever a single bit is $1$, and the identity $I$ wherever it is $0$.\n"
"Then we have\n"
"$$\n"
" X_a X_b  {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kailangan din nating i-implement ang isang bitstring shift.\n"
"Tinutukoy natin ang operator sa $x$ register $X^{a_1}\\cdots X^{a_m}$ bilang $X_a$\n"
"at gayundin sa $y$ register $X_b =  X^{b_1}\\cdots X^{b_m}$.\n"
"Ang mga operator na ito ay naglalapat ng $X$ kung saan ang isang single bit ay $1$, at ang identity $I$ kung saan ito ay $0$.\n"
"Pagkatapos ay mayroon tayo\n"
"$$\n"
" X_a X_b  {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second black box $g$ is implemented by the unitary $U_g$, given by\n"
"$$\n"
"%U_g {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = X_aX_b \\CZ_{x,y} X_aX_b {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"U_g = X_aX_b {CZ}_{x,y} X_aX_b.\n"
"$$\n"
"To see this, we apply the operators from right to left to the state ${|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}$.\n"
"First\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangalawang black box $g$ ay ipinatupad ng unitary $U_g$, na ibinigay ng\n"
"$$\n"
"%U_g {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = X_aX_b \\CZ_{x,y} X_aX_b {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"U_g = X_aX_b {CZ}_{x,y} X_aX_b.\n"
"$$\n"
"Upang makita ito, inilalapat natin ang mga operators mula kanan hanggang kaliwa sa state ${|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}$.\n"
"Una\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" X_a X_b  {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" X_a X_b  {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle} = {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then,\n"
"$$\n"
"  {CZ}_{x,y}  {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle} = (-1)^{(x+a)\\cdot (y+b)} {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos,\n"
"$$\n"
"  {CZ}_{x,y}  {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle} = (-1)^{(x+a)\\cdot (y+b)} {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Finally,\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  X^a X^b (-1)^{(x+a)\\cdot (y+b)} {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle} = (-1)^{(x+a)\\cdot (y+b)} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  X^a X^b (-1)^{(x+a)\\cdot (y+b)} {|{x+a}\\rangle}{|{y+b}\\rangle} = (-1)^{(x+a)\\cdot (y+b)} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which is indeed the quantum version of $f(x+a, y+b)$.\n"
msgstr "na tunay na ang quantum version ng $f(x+a, y+b)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The hidden shift algorithm {#the-hidden-shift-algorithm}"
msgstr "Ang hidden shift algorithm {#the-hidden-shift-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we put the pieces together to solve the hidden shift problem.\n"
"We begin by applying Hadamards to the registers initialized to the all-zero state.\n"
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes 2m} = H^{\\otimes m} \\otimes H^{\\otimes m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{x \\cdot y} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay pinagsasama natin ang mga piraso upang malutas ang hidden shift problem.\n"
"Nagsisimula tayo sa pag-apply ng mga Hadamards sa mga registers na sinimulan sa all-zero state.\n"
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes 2m} = H^{\\otimes m} \\otimes H^{\\otimes m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{x \\cdot y} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we query the oracle $g$ to arrive at\n"
"$$\n"
"U_g H^{\\otimes 2m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{(x+a) \\cdot (y+b)} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\approx \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{x \\cdot y + x \\cdot b + y \\cdot a} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"In the last line, we omitted the constant global phase factor $(-1)^{a \\cdot b}$,\n"
"and denote equality up to a phase by $\\approx$.\n"
"Next, applying the oracle $f$ introduces another factor of $(-1)^{x \\cdot y}$, canceling the one already\n"
"present. We then have:\n"
"$$\n"
"U_f U_g H^{\\otimes 2m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}\n"
"\\approx \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{x \\cdot b + y \\cdot a} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"The final step is to apply the inverse Fourier transform, $H^{\\otimes 2m} = H^{\\otimes m} \\otimes H^{\\otimes m}$,\n"
"resulting in\n"
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes 2m} U_f U_g  H^{\\otimes 2m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}\n"
"\\approx {|{b}\\rangle}{|{a}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"The circuit is finished. In the absence of noise, sampling the quantum registers will\n"
"return the bitstrings $b, a$ with probability $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, i-query natin ang oracle $g$ upang makarating sa\n"
"$$\n"
"U_g H^{\\otimes 2m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{(x+a) \\cdot (y+b)} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\approx \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{x \\cdot y + x \\cdot b + y \\cdot a} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Sa huling linya, inalis natin ang constant global phase factor $(-1)^{a \\cdot b}$,\n"
"at tinutukoy ang pagkakapantay-pantay hanggang sa phase bilang $\\approx$.\n"
"Susunod, ang pag-apply ng oracle $f$ ay nagpapakilala ng isa pang factor ng $(-1)^{x \\cdot y}$, na nagkakansela sa isa nang naroroon.\n"
"Mayroon tayo:\n"
"$$\n"
"U_f U_g H^{\\otimes 2m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}\n"
"\\approx \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{2m}}} \\sum_{x, y \\in {\\mathbb{Z}_2^m}} (-1)^{x \\cdot b + y \\cdot a} {|{x}\\rangle}{|{y}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Ang huling hakbang ay ilapat ang inverse Fourier transform, $H^{\\otimes 2m} = H^{\\otimes m} \\otimes H^{\\otimes m}$,\n"
"na nagreresulta sa\n"
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes 2m} U_f U_g  H^{\\otimes 2m} {{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}{{|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes m}}\n"
"\\approx {|{b}\\rangle}{|{a}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Ang circuit ay tapos na. Sa kawalan ng ingay, ang pag-sample ng quantum registers ay\n"
"magbabalik ng mga bitstrings $b, a$ na may probabilidad na $1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Boolean inner product is an example of the so-called bent functions.\n"
"We will not define bent functions here\n"
"but merely note that they\n"
"\"are maximally resistant against attacks that seek to exploit a dependence of\n"
"the outputs on some linear subspace of the inputs.\"\n"
"This quote is from the article [_Quantum algorithms for highly non-linear Boolean functions_](https://arxiv.org/abs/0811.3208), which\n"
"gives efficient hidden shift algorithms for several classes of bent functions.\n"
"The algorithm in this tutorial appears in Section 3.1 of the article.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Boolean inner product ay isang halimbawa ng tinatawag na bent functions.\n"
"Hindi natin tutukuyin ang mga bent functions dito\n"
"ngunit pansinin lamang na sila\n"
"\"ay maximally resistant laban sa mga atake na naghahangad na samantalahin ang dependensya ng\n"
"mga outputs sa ilang linear subspace ng mga inputs.\"\n"
"Ang quote na ito ay mula sa artikulong [_Quantum algorithms for highly non-linear Boolean functions_](https://arxiv.org/abs/0811.3208), na\n"
"nagbibigay ng mahusay na hidden shift algorithms para sa ilang klase ng bent functions.\n"
"Ang algorithm sa tutorial na ito ay lumalabas sa Section 3.1 ng artikulo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the more general case, the circuit for finding a hidden shift $s \\in \\mathbb{Z}^n$ is\n"
"$$\n"
" H^{\\otimes n} U_{\\tilde{f}}  H^{\\otimes n} U_g  H^{\\otimes n} {|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes n} = {|{s}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
" In the general case, $f$ and $g$ are functions of a single variable.\n"
" Our example of the inner product has this form if we let $f(x, y) \\to f(z)$,\n"
" with $z$ equal to the concatenation of $x$ and $y$, and $s$ equal to the concatenation\n"
" of $a$ and $b$.\n"
" The general case requires exactly two oracles: One oracle for $g$ and one for $\\tilde{f}$,\n"
" where the latter is a function known as the _dual_ of the bent function $f$.\n"
" The inner product function has the self-dual property $\\tilde{f}=f$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas pangkalahatang kaso, ang circuit para sa paghahanap ng hidden shift $s \\in \\mathbb{Z}^n$ ay\n"
"$$\n"
" H^{\\otimes n} U_{\\tilde{f}}  H^{\\otimes n} U_g  H^{\\otimes n} {|{0}\\rangle}^{\\otimes n} = {|{s}\\rangle}.\n"
"$$\n"
" Sa pangkalahatang kaso, ang $f$ at $g$ ay mga functions ng isang solong variable.\n"
" Ang ating halimbawa ng inner product ay may ganitong anyo kung hayaan nating $f(x, y) \\to f(z)$,\n"
" na may $z$ na katumbas ng concatenation ng $x$ at $y$, at $s$ na katumbas ng concatenation\n"
" ng $a$ at $b$.\n"
" Ang pangkalahatang kaso ay nangangailangan ng eksaktong dalawang oracles: Isang oracle para sa $g$ at isa para sa $\\tilde{f}$,\n"
" kung saan ang huli ay isang function na kilala bilang _dual_ ng bent function $f$.\n"
" Ang inner product function ay may self-dual property $\\tilde{f}=f$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
" In our circuit for the hidden shift on the inner product we omitted the middle layer\n"
" of Hadamards that appears in the circuit for the general case. While in the general case\n"
" this layer is necessary, we saved a bit of depth by omitting it, at the expense of a bit\n"
" of post-processing because the output is ${|{b}\\rangle}{|{a}\\rangle}$ instead of the desired ${|{a}\\rangle}{|{b}\\rangle}$.\n"
msgstr ""
" Sa ating circuit para sa hidden shift sa inner product, inalis natin ang gitnang layer\n"
" ng mga Hadamards na lumalabas sa circuit para sa pangkalahatang kaso. Habang sa pangkalahatang kaso\n"
" ang layer na ito ay kailangan, nakatipid tayo ng kaunting depth sa pag-alis nito, sa gastos ng kaunting\n"
" post-processing dahil ang output ay ${|{b}\\rangle}{|{a}\\rangle}$ sa halip na ninanais na ${|{a}\\rangle}{|{b}\\rangle}$.\n"

